Cartouche third-party licenses
=============================

What Cartouche ships or builds from, and under which license. Read by users,
packagers and reviewers. NOTICE explains the licensing of the repository itself.
This file lists the components. Where a license text is in the repository, this
file names the path.

Cartouche is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 (GPL-3.0),
see LICENSE. It started as a fork of NotProton (GPL-3.0) by NotProtonNot and the
NotProton contributors, and is now its own project, not built on NotProton. It
is not affiliated with NotProton, Valve, Apple or CodeWeavers.

Game Porting Toolkit and D3DMetal
---------------------------------

Cartouche does not ship Apple's Game Porting Toolkit or D3DMetal, and no file
from either is in the repository, in a release or in a download that Cartouche
hosts. When the user has their own copy, the app either copies it, at run time,
into the runners folder on the user's Mac, or reads it in place where the user
installed it (a mounted Apple image, a Game Porting Toolkit app, a Homebrew keg
or a folder the user picked). The release workflow scans the app and its zip, and the wine-crossover
workflow its archive, for these files,
by name, by SHA-256 and inside tar archives (packaging/redist-scan.sh,
packaging/redist-hashes.txt).

